# 8. White-labelling

```json
// agencies.branding
{
  "logo_url": "...", "logo_dark_url": "...",
  "primary": "#2B4ACB", "accent": "#0F7A4F",
  "email_from_name": "RyzeWorks", "email_reply_to": "hello@ryzeworks.in",
  "portal_title": "RyzeWorks Client Portal",
  "hide_creo_branding": true
}
```

Resolve the tenant from, in order: custom domain → subdomain slug → JWT claim. Cache the
resolution in Redis for 5 minutes keyed by host. Inject the branding as CSS custom
properties at the layout root so **no component reads the agency object** — they read
tokens, exactly as in the UI system spec.

Client-facing emails send from the agency's name and reply-to. A client of RyzeWorks
should never see the word Creo unless the agency wants them to.

---

# 9. Two billing layers — do not merge them

```
YOU  ──charges──▶  AGENCY     platform subscription (per seat / per client tier)
AGENCY ──charges──▶ CLIENT    the ₹25k / ₹50k / ₹95k retainers
```

Separate tables, separate gateways, separate webhooks. The existing `subscriptions` and
`payment_events` handle agency→client. Add `platform_subscriptions` and
`platform_payment_events` for you→agency.

An agency going `past_due` on **your** invoice must not stop **their** clients' content
from publishing — that punishes someone who paid their bill. Degrade instead: block new
client creation, block new cycle generation, keep existing cycles publishing, show a
banner to agency staff only. Suspend fully only after a stated grace period.

